note S4 unsized views (spec 6, erratum E2): sized arrays, an unsized name and a text passed to `view T *`
note and `edit T *` parameters of internal functions, inline ones included; `len` is the run-time count
note (ulong); constant and run-time indexes in range; a write slice inside the view; six parameter slots
note mixing scalars and unsized arrays (pointer then count). Exit 0 when every check holds, else the
note failing check's number.
om2
text msg "abcdef"
fn vsum v view ulong * to ulong
x = ulong 0
for i ulong len v
x = add x get v i
end
ret x
end
fn pass v view ulong * to ulong
ret vsum v
end
fn isum v view ulong * to ulong inline
ret add get v 0 get v sub len v 1
end
fn fill e edit uchar * c uchar to ulong
for i ulong len e
put e i add c uchar i
end
ret len e
end
fn six a ulong v view ulong * b ulong w edit uchar * to ulong
put w 0 uchar b
ret add add mul a 1000 len v add mul b 100 len w
end
fn bytes t view uchar * to ulong
ret add mul ulong get t 0 256 len t
end
fn sl a ulong v view uchar * b ulong to ulong
ret add add mul a 100 mul len v 10 b
end
fn main to int
u = new uchar 7 0
if ne sl 3 u 4 374
ret 10
end
a = new ulong 5 3
put a 4 10
if ne vsum a 22
ret 1
end
if ne pass a 22
ret 2
end
if ne isum a 13
ret 3
end
if ne fill u 40 7
ret 4
end
if ne get u 6 46
ret 5
end
if ne six 2 a 9 u 2912
ret 6
end
if ne get u 0 9
ret 7
end
if ne bytes msg 24838
ret 8
end
if ne bytes view u 2311
ret 9
end
ret 0
end
